WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.067
Packaging with pyproject dot toml.

2
00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:06.733
This is how loose scripts become real, installable code.

3
00:00:07.933 --> 00:00:12.167
A pyproject dot toml file describes your project in one place.

4
00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.367
Name, version, dependencies, and the build backend.

5
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:21.267
It turns code into an installable unit, and it ends the old habit of hacking sys dot path.

6
00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:23.700
Here is a real one.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.533
The project table holds the name, version, Python requirement, and runtime dependencies.

8
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:35.433
Optional dependency groups keep tools like pytest and mypy out of production installs.

9
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:38.600
And the build system names the backend that builds it.

10
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:40.867
Now the magic.

11
00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:45.300
With a pyproject in your repo, you run pip install dash e dot.

12
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.100
That's an editable install.

13
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:52.767
Your package is now importable from anywhere on the machine, and edits take effect immediately.

14
00:00:53.967 --> 00:00:55.167
Two more habits help.

15
00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:58.867
Install the dev group on demand with the extras syntax.

16
00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:04.233
And use a src layout, so you can't import your code by accident without installing it.

17
00:01:05.433 --> 00:01:06.733
Here's a real story.

18
00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:13.533
The same API client code was copy-pasted into the agent repo and the FastAPI repo.

19
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:16.633
Until a pagination bug had to be fixed twice.

20
00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:24.100
Extracted as orbital tools, one fix reaches both, and the editable install keeps iteration friction at zero.

21
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:26.130
Let's recap.

22
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.967
Pyproject dot toml declares your package.

23
00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:32.300
An editable install makes it importable everywhere.

24
00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:35.133
Optional groups keep dev tools out of production.

25
00:01:35.433 --> 00:01:38.805
And one package means one fix for every consumer.

26
00:01:38.805 --> 00:01:40.800
Next up: unit testing basics.
